cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StepScope in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "StepScope: a research toolkit for post-training dynamics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Zepeng
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lexwzp0/stepscope"
abstract: >-
  StepScope treats one real parameter update as the basic object of study: for any backbone,
  post-training objective and optimizer it measures the actual change of differentiable
  observables between checkpoints, predicts it to first order along the measured update, and
  reports the calibration of that prediction. Per-source decomposition, LDCL interaction
  channels, behaviour and representation analyses are plugins on fixed tables.
